WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:22.643
Luckily the princess had also told the children how to make her reappear.

2
00:00:22.644 --> 00:00:27.974
"If we close our eyes," said Gerald, "she'll reappear when we count to fifty.

3
00:00:27.975 --> 00:00:33.676
One, two, three, four . . ."

4
00:00:33.677 --> 00:00:38.971
Gerald and Kathleen closed their eyes, but Jimmy kept his open.

5
00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:44.150
Soon he saw a panel under the window slowly open.

6
00:00:44.151 --> 00:00:46.260
"I knew it was a trick,"

7
00:00:46.261 --> 00:00:51.561
he thought before he closed his eyes.

8
00:00:51.562 --> 00:00:54.714
At fifty the children opened their eyes.

9
00:00:54.715 --> 00:00:57.531
But there was still no princess.

10
00:00:57.532 --> 00:01:01.879
"I think there's a secret cupboard under the window," said Jimmy.

11
00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.713
"Maybe she's hiding in it."

12
00:01:04.714 --> 00:01:09.593
"You looked! That's cheating!" said the voice of the princess.

13
00:01:09.594 --> 00:01:13.263
The voice was so close to Jimmy's ear that he jumped.

14
00:01:13.264 --> 00:01:16.180
But the princess was still invisible.

15
00:01:16.181 --> 00:01:20.980
"Where is she?" cried all three children at once.

16
00:01:20.981 --> 00:01:25.783
"Should we close our eyes and count again?" asked Kathleen.

17
00:01:25.784 --> 00:01:29.883
"Don't be silly!" The princess sounded angry.

18
00:01:29.884 --> 00:01:32.765
"We're not silly," said Jimmy.

19
00:01:32.765 --> 00:01:34.634
"We know you're hiding."

20
00:01:34.635 --> 00:01:37.795
"You think you're so clever pretending not to see me."

21
00:01:37.796 --> 00:01:40.052
The princess sounded hurt.

22
00:01:40.053 --> 00:01:42.416
"All right, I'll play your game."

23
00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:46.159
"But we can't see you," said Gerald.

24
00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.647
"Really?" The princess sounded afraid now.

25
00:01:49.648 --> 00:01:52.760
"We told you that," said Jimmy.

26
00:01:52.761 --> 00:01:55.739
He suddenly leaned backward and forward.

27
00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.881
Then it happened again.

28
00:01:57.882 --> 00:02:01.268
"What's wrong?" asked Kathleen.

29
00:02:01.269 --> 00:02:03.487
"She shook me!"

30
00:02:03.488 --> 00:02:07.659
"And I'll shake him again if he says he can't see me."

31
00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.650
"What are you so grumpy about?"

32
00:02:09.651 --> 00:02:11.947
Gerald was quite calm.

33
00:02:11.948 --> 00:02:15.291
"You said you'd be invisible and you are."

34
00:02:15.292 --> 00:02:19.551
"I'm not. You're just pretending not to see me."

35
00:02:19.552 --> 00:02:25.841
"On my word of honor, you're still invisible," said Gerald.

36
00:02:25.842 --> 00:02:28.165
There was silence.

37
00:02:28.166 --> 00:02:31.122
Then the princess said, "Come, I'll let you out.

38
00:02:31.123 --> 00:02:35.356
I'm tired of playing with you."

39
00:02:35.357 --> 00:02:39.239
They followed her voice out of the treasure room.

40
00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.846
She led them through some other rooms.

41
00:02:43.847 --> 00:02:46.733
One room was lined with mirrors.

42
00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:50.756
Gerald suddenly said to the princess, "Give me your hand."

43
00:02:50.757 --> 00:02:53.521
He pulled her in front of a mirror.

44
00:02:53.522 --> 00:02:56.254
"Now look for yourself."

45
00:02:56.255 --> 00:02:59.850
"Oh!" cried the princess in despair.

46
00:02:59.851 --> 00:03:03.498
"I am invisible. What shall I do?"

47
00:03:03.499 --> 00:03:07.005
"Take the ring off," said Kathleen.

48
00:03:07.006 --> 00:03:08.830
"It won't come off!

49
00:03:08.831 --> 00:03:10.293
But it can't be the ring.

50
00:03:10.294 --> 00:03:12.810
Rings don't make you invisible."

51
00:03:12.811 --> 00:03:16.645
"You said this one did," said Kathleen.

52
00:03:16.646 --> 00:03:18.886
"I was only playing at magic.

53
00:03:18.887 --> 00:03:21.634
I just hid in the secret cupboard."

54
00:03:21.635 --> 00:03:25.774
"But you can do magic," said Gerald.

55
00:03:25.775 --> 00:03:28.433
"What about the jewels?"

56
00:03:28.434 --> 00:03:32.562
"That's only a secret button that makes the panels open.

57
00:03:32.563 --> 00:03:34.442
What shall I do?"

58
00:03:34.443 --> 00:03:36.816
The princess was crying.

59
00:03:36.817 --> 00:03:41.975
Kathleen moved toward the voice and wrapped her arms around the invisible princess.

60
00:03:41.976 --> 00:03:46.398
"I'll tell the king and queen."

61
00:03:46.399 --> 00:03:49.593
"But they were only a game like . . ."

62
00:03:49.594 --> 00:03:54.458
"The bread and cheese," Jimmy said triumphantly.

63
00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:57.505
"And the story I told you in the maze.

64
00:03:57.506 --> 00:04:02.071
I wasn't really asleep for a hundred years."

65
00:04:02.072 --> 00:04:04.492
The princess sniffed.

66
00:04:04.493 --> 00:04:10.091
"But if you're not the princess, who are you?" said Kathleen.

67
00:04:10.092 --> 00:04:11.896
"My aunt works here.

68
00:04:11.897 --> 00:04:14.122
She'll be angry if she finds you.

69
00:04:14.123 --> 00:04:16.341
Run outside to the Temple of Flora.

70
00:04:16.342 --> 00:04:20.229
I'll meet you there after I close up the treasure room."

71
00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.570
The three children went to the Temple of Flora.

72
00:04:23.571 --> 00:04:26.482
It was cool and restful inside.

73
00:04:26.483 --> 00:04:31.396
Soon they heard footsteps and saw a shadow on the ground.

74
00:04:31.397 --> 00:04:36.408
"The door to the treasure room has blown shut," said the princess.

75
00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:40.607
"It's locked and the key's inside!"

76
00:04:40.608 --> 00:04:44.664
"Sit down and we'll talk about what to do," said Gerald.

77
00:04:44.665 --> 00:04:49.166
"But first tell us your name."

78
00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:54.913
"My . . . my name is Mabel Prowse."

79
00:04:54.914 --> 00:04:58.538
The princess' voice was broken with sobs.

80
00:04:58.539 --> 00:05:08.633
"And . . . and I'm the housekeeper's niece at the castle!"
